<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · religion</p><h1 class="enc-title">Quakers</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Religious Society of Friends, Friends</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Quakers, or Religious Society of Friends, are a Christian movement founded by George Fox in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> in the 1650s. They reject clergy and formal sacraments and meet in silent worship, waiting for the 'inner light'. Persecuted in England, many emigrated to America, where <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-penn">William Penn</a> founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pennsylvania">Pennsylvania</a>, and Quakers became leading campaigners against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavery">slavery</a> and for peace.</p></div>
